Gaps found for MCPD/MPSD/MSTD config (MDLL excluded).

Real bugs (config schema accepts it, hardware never gets it):

- MSTD-16 is unconfigured. `MesyModuleConfig::Mstd { threshold, gain }` exists,
  but `set_up_module()` only matches `Mpsd8SADC | Mpsd8 | Mpsd8P`; `Mstd16`/
  `Mstd16P` fall into the `other` arm (warn + skip). Wiring it up properly
  also needs: 16 channels (not 8) for per-channel gain, the separate
  `SETGAIN_MSTD` (cmd 26) command on newer firmware vs. `SETGAIN_MPSD` with a
  "channel index >7 gets halved" quirk on old firmware, and MSTD's differing
  pulser/mode defaults.

- `Mpsd8Old` (module type 1) is likewise unconfigured -- same match-arm gap,
  same silent-skip warning.

Missing feature (has a TODO already):

- Position/amplitude mode (`SETMODE`, cmd 16) isn't implemented -- no
  `Cmd::SetMode` variant exists; `MesyModuleConfig` has `// TODO amp mode`.
  Needed for MPSD-8/MPSD-8old hardware that can only stream one of
  position-or-amplitude at a time (MPSD-8+ can do both simultaneously, which
  is what the existing TX-mode capability negotiation covers).

Missing feature (no hook to configure it at all):

- Aux timers (`SETAUXTIMER`, cmd 10) aren't implemented. `CellTrigger` lets a
  cell select `Aux1..Aux4` as its trigger source, but nothing configures what
  period each aux timer actually runs at.

Lower priority / probably not worth chasing:

- `SETPARAM`/`GETPARAM` (per-buffer header "parameter" values: monitor/ADC/
  counter/clock sources) aren't exposed.

- `SETRUNID` isn't pushed to hardware; `run_id` stays a host-side/file-naming
  concept only.
